{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For the third day.</b> That is the day of Shabbat, the day of the giving of the Torah — third from this day, which is the fourth of the month and the fifth of the week, for on that third day <b>He descended</b> etc. Since He did not specify for you here a time for this warning, He specified it for them in another place: 'Go say to them: return to your tents.' And some say 'Moses told' (ויגד משה) is the same as 'Moses returned' (וישב משה) above, but the sequence of days is not reconciled according to the verses, neither according to the Rabbis nor according to Rabbi Yosi."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The abbreviations ד׳ and ה׳‎ here refer to the day of the month and day of the week respectively, not divine names; resolved by context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:47.570490497Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}